> When doing a sacfest as a chaotic, how do people handle peaceful monsters
> from /oCrMon etc.? I know there's an alignment penalty (bigger if you kill
> them in one shot, right? so don't do that) but if you've been killing lots
> of creatures and you're pretty sure you started at 20, it's probably OK to
> kill and #offer one peaceful? Just want to make sure there is not some
> additional penalty for #offer'ing the corpse of a formerly peaceful
> monster; the alignment penalty at kill time is the only issue, correct?
> (Plus the special scenario of #offer'ing own race.)

As long as you start the fest with numerical alignment high
enough the alignment hit for any one peaceful monster is not
enough to be a problem.  The problem is when you've killed
a bunch of peacefuls consequatively.  Also as long as you
kill about 3-4 hostiles per peaceful your numerical alignment
will trend up enough that killing one more hostile will handle
any problem of killing a peaceful (with certain exceptions).

So when doing a sacfest as a chaotic I make a point to kill
several consequative hotiles before starting then whack
whatever arrives.  It works fine.  Just know the exceptions to
nopt kill.

For that matter some of the exceptions have good specific
uses.


